<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94693" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπ-ας</span></b> , gen. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					857
				</span></i>
			: τό: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπω</span>):—<i>covering, shelter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κὰδ δ᾽ ἄρ᾽ Ὀδυσσῆ᾽ εἷσαν
				ἐπὶ σκέπας</span> placed him in or under <i>shelter</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				6.212
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				210
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἀνέμοιο</span>
			<i>shelter</i> from the wind, <i><span class="en">
				5.443
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.336
			</span></i>: abs. in poet. nom. and acc. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπᾰ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				532
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπας ὅρμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					736
				</span></i>
			; of clothes, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλαίνης λιτὸν
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.43
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Parmen.
			</span></i>); of the <i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i> hat (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυσία</span>), ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.335
			</span></i> (Antip. Thess.): pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωσάμενοι σκέπασι λινοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					4.12
				</span></i>
			 codd. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκεπάσμασι</span> is prob.
			l.): metaph. in sg., <i>pretext, pretence</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Antiop.</u>
			</span></i> iv <i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				2
			</span></i> Arnim.—In Prose commonly <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπη</span> (q.v.), or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπασμα</span>.</div>
